SURVIVORSHIP -- why the table above cannot be read at face value.
`relative_strike` is ATM-RELATIVE, so a strike pinned at entry is only quoted
while spot stays near it. An exit that fails to price is missing BECAUSE the
market ran away from the strike -- and for a SHORT call spread, spot running up
is the losing direction. Below, how much of the sample that quietly removes:
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
  exit      quoted%     n quoted    n imputed
  2h          56.2%      290,568      516,958
  EOD         34.9%      176,607      505,419
  2d          25.1%      119,390      475,408
  5d          15.5%       59,956      386,357

  The repair: at expiry an option IS its intrinsic, so a vanished leg is worth
  max(spot - strike, 0) with no quote at all. Checked against the strikes that
  WERE still quoted at the bell, that rule lands within one tick (median
  Rs+0.05) -- see bell_intrinsic_check.py.

